    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n58219" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κνίψ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ </span>(ἡ
		v.l. in
		<i><span class="en">
			Arist.
		</span></i>, v. infr.), gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κνῑπός</span>, nom. pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κνῖπες,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκνίψ</span>
			, small creatures which infest fig and oak trees and devour the
			fig-insect (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψήν</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				590
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				534b19
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				2.8.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				4.14.10
			</span></i>; small ants acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Sens.</u>
				444b12
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> pl., 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄμματα περιβεβρωμένα</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
